# Ingestion runtime for transport: tcp — the stock image plus the one dependency
# the native binding needs. Everything else about the dev loop is unchanged: the
# connector itself still arrives as a bind-mount on PYTHONPATH, so connector edits
# need no rebuild; only a change of the library pin does.
# The base image is an ARGUMENT because two things about it vary per site, and
# neither is a reason to fork this file.
#
# REGISTRY. The same image is published to both registries, and it is the same
# bytes -- not a mirror that can drift. For linux/amd64,
# `openmetadata/ingestion:2.0.1.0` and
# `docker.getcollate.io/openmetadata/ingestion:2.0.1.0` both resolve to
# sha256:42a3c912..., and the 2.0.2 pair both resolve to sha256:aca874af...
# (`docker manifest inspect` each and compare). So a network that cannot reach
# getcollate.io -- a corporate proxy, a locked-down WSL -- only needs the other
# name.
#
# VERSION. This image must match the OpenMetadata the ingestion runs into; the
# SDK requirement in pyproject.toml is a RANGE precisely so the image's own SDK
# survives. Upstream tags are not shaped alike -- compare
# `openmetadata/ingestion:2.0.1.0` with `openmetadata/ingestion:2.0.2` -- and a
# version is always written here as part of an image reference, because the leak
# gate reads a bare four-part one as an IPv4 address and refuses the file.
#
#   docker build -t ssas-ingestion:tcp -f docker/Dockerfile.tcp docker/ \
#     --build-arg BASE_IMAGE=openmetadata/ingestion:2.0.2
#
# The default stays the Collate registry at the version compose.yml and CI use;
# a default that disagrees with them is its own kind of trap.
ARG BASE_IMAGE=docker.getcollate.io/openmetadata/ingestion:2.0.1.0
FROM ${BASE_IMAGE}

USER root
# `python -m pip`, not `pip`: the image's pip is a wrapper that refuses to run as
# root, and installing as airflow would write into a directory it does not own.
# ssas-xmla-tcp is not on PyPI, hence the git URL. The ref is an ARG pinned to a
# TAG, not a branch: an image built from @main is not reproducible, so the same
# build command two weeks apart could install different libraries without saying
# so -- which is what the pinning discipline elsewhere in this repo exists to
# prevent. Keep it in step with the [tcp] extra in pyproject.toml, and pass
# --build-arg SSAS_XMLA_REF=main only to test a fix that is not released yet.
# It pulls exactly one dependency of its own (pyspnego).
ARG SSAS_XMLA_REF=v0.1.2
RUN python -m pip install --no-cache-dir \
      "ssas-xmla-tcp @ git+https://github.com/oluies/ssas-xmla-tcp@${SSAS_XMLA_REF}"

# Back to the image's own user — the ingestion runtime expects to be airflow.
USER airflow
